\textbf{Definition 12} (KDM-ATK secure encryption)\textbf{.} \emph{For}
ATK \emph{∈\{}CPA\emph{,} CCA\emph{\}, we say a public-}

\emph{key encryption scheme} Π = (Gen\emph{,} Enc\emph{,} Dec) \emph{is}
KDM{[}\emph{F}{]}-ATK \emph{secure if, for every probabilistic}

\emph{polynomial-time adversary A as above and for all n, we have:}

\begin{quote}
Prob{[}ExpKDM-ATK\\
Π\emph{,A,F}

(1\emph{k}) = 1{]} \emph{≤}1 2 + \emph{negl}(\emph{k})\emph{.}
\end{quote}

\textbf{Simulation soundness and CCA-KDM security.} As shown in {[}14,
Appendix A.1{]}, a variation of the Naor-Yung paradigm instantiated with
a simulation-sound NIZK can leverage CPA-security to CCA-security in the
context of KDM security, provided that one of the two encryption scheme
already satisfy KDM-CPA security. The basic elements are an encryption
scheme Π = (Gen\emph{,} Enc\emph{,} Dec) with KDM-CPA security with
respect a given class of function \emph{F}, a CPA-secure encryption
scheme Π\emph{′}= (Gen\emph{′,} Enc\emph{′,} Dec\emph{′}) and a
simulation sound NIZK proofΠ\emph{∗}= (Gen\emph{∗,} Enc\emph{∗,}
Dec\emph{∗}) is defined as in the original NY paradigm of twin
encryption (see system (\emph{PH, VH}) for the NY language associated to
(Π\emph{,} Π\emph{′}). The combined encryption scheme Section D.3).

The statement below is the ROM-equivalent of {[}14{]}. The proof
strategy is essentially the same already used in the proof of Theorem 5,
the only difference being the instantiation of Πwith a KDM-CPA scheme.

\textbf{Theorem 6} (ROM-equivalent of {[}14{]})\textbf{.} \emph{Let} Π
\emph{be a KDM-CPA secure encryption scheme with respect to a class of
function F,} Π\emph{′be a CPA-secure encryption scheme and let}
(\emph{PH, VH}) \emph{be a simulation-sound NIZK proof system for the
Naor-Yung language LNY associated to} (Π\emph{,} Π\emph{′})\emph{. In
the random oracle model, the encryption scheme} Π\emph{∗obtained via the
Naor-Yung paradigm is KDM-CCA secure with respect to the class of
function F.}

\emph{Proof.} We only sketch the proof. Consider the KDM-CCA experiment
adapted for the NY construction:

